# .pseudonyms.env.example — committed. Holds NO clearnames.
#
# Copy to `.pseudonyms.env` (gitignored) and fill in the real names there.
# On the prod server: copy the filled file over after the github-ops, then
#   scripts/pseudonyms.py deanon <paths> --write
#
#   CODE="Canonical Clearname|another surface|Lastname"
#
# The FIRST surface is canonical — `deanon` writes it back. The rest are extra
# spellings `check`/`anon` must also catch. Matching is case-insensitive and
# whole-word, longest surface first, so a full name is consumed before its parts.
#
# Codes are house style: 5 characters, derived the way Julku came from Julia.
# Keep any code that already circulates in the docs rather than re-minting it.

# EXAMPL="Full Name|Firstname|Lastname"

# Guard it in CI or as a pre-commit hook:
#   scripts/pseudonyms.py check --staged
